      <details class="tp-faq"><summary><h3>What is the golden ratio for a face?</h3></summary><p>The golden ratio is about 1.618. The most cited facial version is face length about 1.618 times face width, with the mouth about 1.618 times as wide as the nose.</p></details>
      <details class="tp-faq"><summary><h3>What is a good golden ratio face score?</h3></summary><p>Most real faces score between about 70% and 90% on this calculator. A high score means your proportions are close to the classic targets, not that you are more attractive.</p></details>
      <details class="tp-faq"><summary><h3>Do beautiful faces follow the golden ratio?</h3></summary><p>Studies have not found that attractive faces cluster around 1.618. Attractive faces tend to be close to the population average and fairly symmetrical.</p></details>
